# Customer Churn Analysis

## 📊 Project Overview
This project analyzes customer behavior data to identify patterns behind customer churn (cancellation of subscriptions). The goal is to understand why customers leave and suggest ways to improve retention.

---

## 🛠️ Tools Used
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn

---

## 📌 Steps Performed
1. Imported and cleaned the dataset
2. Performed Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
3. Analyzed customer churn distribution
4. Studied relationship between churn and features like tenure and monthly charges
5. Visualized important patterns using graphs
6. Extracted insights from data

---

## 📈 Key Insights
- Customers with low tenure are more likely to churn
- Higher monthly charges increase churn probability
- Low engagement customers tend to leave more often

---

## 💡 Recommendations
- Offer discounts for new customers
- Improve onboarding experience
- Provide loyalty rewards for long-term users
- Introduce flexible pricing plans

---

## 🚀 Outcome
This analysis helps identify key factors affecting customer retention and provides actionable insights to reduce churn rate.
